Subject: [PATCH 4/5] P1-42 / U-70: preview engine probe must cross the
 u8path_compat boundary like ensureEngine()

Finding U-70 (F:NF-13, fix-order P1-42, state OPEN at main fe4f0a7):

    Preview engine check bypasses UTF-8 boundary — ensureEngine() wraps
    u8path_compat(), startPreview() passes raw enginePath_.toStdString()
    to path_is_executable().

The codebase rule (src/core/WinUnicode.h, PRODUCT CONSTRAINTS in
SESSION_HANDOFF): every std::string <-> fs::path boundary goes through
u8path_compat / path_u8string — the conversion layer that exists for
legacy-ACP Windows hosts, where the bare form throws or splits on
non-UTF-8 input. ensureEngine() honours it; startPreview()'s engine
re-probe did not, so the preview path could fail (or throw) on exactly the
hosts U-07 fixed the CLI for, while the main-run path worked — a
mode-dependent honesty difference.

One-line behavioural change: probe through the same wrapper the main run
uses. (The "cancelling lifetime" half of F:NF-15 lands separately — that
is the U-72 latch patch; P1-42 groups the two.)

Proof plan (Qt-class row — CI proves what a no-Qt sandbox cannot):

  * cmake build clean on linux + windows (both CI GUI steps).
  * Offscreen harness T-cases unchanged-green.
  * Sentinel (CI): grep -c 'gs::u8path_compat(enginePath_.toStdString())'
    src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp >= 3 (two in ensureEngine, one in startPreview)
    and no bare 'path_is_executable(enginePath_' remains.
  * New harness case T23 (sketch in the accompanying audit MD): with
    GS_ENGINE pointed at a path under a non-ASCII directory, a preview run
    must reach the engine instead of reporting "engine not found". Needs a
    Qt host; CI's offscreen run is the executor.

After green CI proof: §5 row U-70 -> FIXED (harness: T23 (offscreen) +
sentinel), P1-42 -> DONE together with the U-72 sibling, then
check_docs.sh --emit + G10 base re-anchor.
---
 .../gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp         | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp b/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp
index 2222222..3333333 100644
--- a/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp
+++ b/working_code/gifscythe/src/qtui/MainWindow.cpp
@@ -617,7 +617,13 @@ void MainWindow::startPreview() {
     previewPanel_->clearAfter(QStringLiteral("select an existing file to preview"));
     return;
   }
-  if (!gs::path_is_executable(enginePath_.toStdString())) {
+  // U-70 / P1-42 (F:NF-13): the preview path re-probed the engine with a
+  // bare toStdString(), bypassing the u8path_compat boundary that
+  // ensureEngine() wraps — the one std::string -> fs::path conversion this
+  // codebase allows at API edges (it exists for legacy-ACP Windows hosts,
+  // where the bare form throws or splits). One rule everywhere: every
+  // fs::path boundary goes through u8path_compat.
+  if (!gs::path_is_executable(gs::u8path_compat(enginePath_.toStdString()))) {
     previewPanel_->clearAfter(QStringLiteral("engine not found — preview unavailable"));
     return;
   }
